wner as a rule-versus-instruction conflict. Everything the owner ruling ordered was executed and I found no fabricated reading: SN-036 drops \"machine-readable\" and \"a check reports\" with need/why untouched; SR-161 re-points to roster + brief + review record with Verification=Inspection and no new cell, carrier or check; LLR-183's NOT DISCHARGED clause is closed by amendment; TC-211 and the procedure now inspect an actual review record instead of an absent producer; hats_no_finding is nowhere built. OI-86/OI-87 are recorded as ruled (a) exactly as the owner record states — no IF change, LLR-041's route already run in 13593db9, and neither row re-approves or re-amends anything."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":85188,"cache_read_input_tokens":835,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":85188},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99e0be93-bcc8-4d2f-bfc7-2ce668e82403","uuid":"efc539e0-38da-4691-88ad-4be2ebb42c6f","request_id":"req_011Ceo51zKeCujfmZrErNzr8"}
